carrier/encoding/container**, a\n35\t  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n36\t  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n37\t  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n38\t  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n39\t  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n40\t  -- yet (nor D19-D21's). D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n41\t  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided\n42\t  item) for network (rows 68/69, built), process (rows 71/72) and file/registry/schedule telemetry (row 74).\n43\t- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n44\t  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar (D18; D17 no host),\n45\t  aspx_inline_csharp (D19: web-page host, file still named `.csx`), jenkins_pipeline + classic_asp (D20; classic_asp wraps\n46\t  VBScript = first host for a PRIOR language, first day with two host files); D21 GitHub Actions came as a LANGUAGE\n47\t  (`polyglot-github_actions`, profile standalone), not a host. D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n48\t  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n49\t  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt),\n50\t  D18 a cloud/SaaS script host (Google Apps Script in a Docs sid