{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FWPPcPD6mekY6P1y1etLP8","type":"tool_result","content":"186\t| 101 | Actor/message-passing flow (Erlang `spawn`/`!`/`receive`, Elixir `send`/`GenServer.call/cast`, Akka `tell`, Go channels, JS `postMessage`/Worker) | gap (D26 prompt \"trace the message flow\"; no code shipped) | `spawn(fun ..)`, `Pid ! {tag, V}`, `receive {tag, X} ->`, `register(name, Pid)`, `gen_server:call`, `handle_cast`; `send(pid, msg)`; `new Worker(`/`onmessage` | gap actor-message-flow-model (static send/receive edge list -> ordered flow) | low |\n187\t\n188\tCounts: 101 rows; seen 37 (rows 1-18, 22, 30 (GHA only), 35, 48-52, 67, 70, 75, 77 (JSP D24; Java/Kotlin gap), 82 (NSIS D22), 89-91 + 94\n189\t(D23), 95 (Elixir D25, Erlang D26)), gap 64 (rows 100-101 opened by D26; rows 96-99 by D24; rows 66, 68, 69, 71, 72, 78-81, 83-86, 88, 92-93, 98-99 have lib support built; 87 given up).\n190\t\n191\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n192\t```\n193\tFINGERPRINT (first 512 bytes + `file`), never by extension:\n194\t FF FE / FE FF / NUL every 2nd byte -> UTF-16: iconv -f UTF-16LE -t UTF-8 first (.reg, PS \"Unicode\" saves, .inf)\n195\t 1F 8B gzip | PK\\x03\\x04 zip/ooxml(.docm .xlsm) | D0 CF 11 E0 OLE(.doc .xls .msi) | ITSF chm | 4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 lnk\n196\t E4 52 5C 7B onenote | \\x1bLua luac | FasdUAS .scpt | MEI\\x0c/PYZ pyinstaller | 0d0d0a pyc | #@~^ Script-Encoder -> wshenc\n197\tSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:\n198\t #!..perl / use strict; / my $descriptor_ -> perl (D15)   DESCRIPTOR_<HEX> = / def build_plan_ / ->(_env) -> ruby (D16)\n199\t #Requires AutoHotkey / x := \"..\" / Map( / ; comments -> autohotkey v2 (D17; family polyglot-auto_hotkey, underscore)\n200\t onOpen_ / DocumentApp / HtmlService / showSidebar / UrlFetchApp -> Google Apps Script (D18; polyglot-google_apps_script)\n201\t ExcelScript./Office.onReady -> Office add-in  \"manifest_version\" -> browser ext  set x \"v\"/proc -> tcl  x <- v -> R  := -> go\n202\t fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   final String x= / def f = { -> / pipeline{ -> groovy (D20)\n203\t BEGIN{ / getline -> awk              target:\\n\\tcmd / $(shell -> make     FROM / RUN -> Dockerfile\n204\t on:/jobs:/runs-on: + `# HUNTRESS..` line 1 + env HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR (no id) -> GH Actions (D21; polyglot-github_actions)\n205\t Name/OutFile/Section + StrCpy $0 \"..\" + `;` marker -> NSIS (D22)  [Setup]/[Code] -> Inno  <Wix>/CustomAction -> WiX/MSI\n206\t stages: -> GitLab  pool: -> Azure  kind: -> k8s  - hosts: -> ansible  local-exec -> terraform  Editor 5.00 -> .reg  $CHICAGO$ -> .inf\n207\t <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n208\t <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild   <%@ Page/runat=\"server\" -> ASPX (D19)   <%@ Language=VBScript %> -> classic ASP (D20)\n209\t <%! String DESCRIPTOR_ -> JSP (D24)  `#`+descriptor_x = +%{..} -> elixir (D25)  `%`+-module(+build_plan() -> \"..\". (no name) -> erlang (D26)\n210\t extends RefCounted / const X: String = / func f() -> Dictionary: / `#` marker -> GDScript (D23)  [gd_scene/[gd_resource -> Godot\n211\t resource (script/source = \"escaped\")  GDPC -> .pck  label start:/init python: -> Ren'Py  game:GetService -> Luau  @\"..\" -> Squirrel\n212\t host-<profile>-<lang> may wrap an OLD language (D20 classic_asp VBScript in a .vbs): marker first, plan says language=\n213\t Sub AutoOpen/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA  =EXEC( -> XLM  __EventFilter -> MOF  #nullable/BuildPlan_ => -> csx (D19)  let/|> -> fsx\n214\tPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n215\t grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n216\t marker with NO data (D18 `:SPLIT`) -> plan = next multi-line literal ARRAY `[ \"FRAG-..\",\"..\",..].join(\"\")`: join, strip\n217\t   `<TAG>-`, peel; other syntaxes: `\"\".join([..])` `-join @(..)` `table.concat({..})` `join('',..)` `Join(Array(..),\"\")`.\n218\t marker data running into `\\n..` / descriptor `= \\\"..\\\"` (D19 ASPX: inner script is an ESCAPED string) -> unescape `\\n \\\" \\\\`\n219\t   (`\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) first\n220\t   (it read D18 + D19), then fix the read -- never walk role/attack enums or put a guessed value in a bulk POST.\n221\t descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n222\t   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n223\t material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n224\t peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n225\t   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n226\t   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n227\t D23 `LYR-<l1>_<l2>_<l3>-data` = ENCODE layers (b64 b32 hex rev frag): undo last-first; obfuscation answer = layer string\n228\t copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code or a known list\n229\tTIMED CONTRACT GRAMMAR (D23): ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` over `<6hex>.<ext>` members -> route by field; composite fields =\n230\t labels joined by `|` in the question's order; indicator = first present in the question's order; campaign-token = after 1st\n231\t `-`; url-host/path-leaf from plan url/file_path; cross-file ids (handoff-id) resolved PER MASTERY SET. Diff id grammar first.\n232\t Still the grammar D26 (TT 1677, M 10 sets; new lang = +13 ids/member). NEXT LANGUAGE = the one leaving the timed pool (3/3).\n233\tLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n234\t PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n235\t JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n236\t VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n237\t Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n238\t XLM xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper | Python: exec->print under python3 -I, marshal->pycdc\n239\t compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n240\t PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\n241\tNEVER run the fixture's interpreter (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File), Deparse/`make -n` (they execute), XSLT, plan URLs.\n242\tSYNTHETIC LABELS: read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`, `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch expansion =\n243\t STATEMENT table (D15+), but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (D23). A carried label rejected on unchanged\n244\t bytes = regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh AND the asking field.\n245\tNETWORK/PROCESS/OUTLIER/WEBSHELL/CONFIG-DRIFT/MESSAGE-FLOW+COLLISION-DECOY prompts (D16-D26): flavour (13/13) unless a question ships;\n246\t then lib.codec network_indicators+reconcile, download_graph; declared_spawns vs process_events -> reconcile_processes.\n247\tATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n248\t .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..Erlang).\n249\t```\n250\t\n251\t## Readiness gaps\n252\tBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D24 nights (see git history) and D25 night\n253\tfind-codecs-speed-gate, beam-erlang-elixir-route, rust-cargo-buildrs-route, terraform-hcl-function-fold, jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier,\n254\twebshell-request-primitive-model, eex-heex-template-carrier, game-archive-carriers. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static,\n255\tevidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route, awk-sed-program-route,\n256\tcomposite-label-field-regime -- the D25-night failures were mostly OTHER lanes' fixture timings under load (android\n257\tlocal_store_scan 4.67 s, xamarin_assembly_scan 2.05-6.10 s > 2 s) plus `__import__()` and `import tomllib` (not in\n258\thctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS: use stdlib parsers already allowed, hand-roll TOML), so the pool-language pairs are\n259\tre-queued under NEW narrow ids. Priority-1 order for D27: the pool sibling pairs (zsh/fish, awk/sed), the Nim/Swift/Tcl\n260\tliteral forms, and the nameless-literal fallback (D22 NSIS + D26 Erlang had no descriptor name); then the D26 narrative\n261\t(collision decoys), compiled BEAM, shell-rc and JVM host twists, the D25 config-survival model, message flow last.\n262\t\n263\t```json\n264\t[\n265\t  {\"id\": \"zsh-fish-minimal-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"zsh and fish v=3 polyglots in the plain D23-D26 shape (narrow re-queue of the given-up zsh-fish-shell-route)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"zsh/fish are a sibling pair still in the 14-language pool after D26 (the last two drops were the BEAM pair Elixir -> Erlang). zsh-fish-shell-route failed twice ONLY on android fixture timing (local_store_scan 4.67 s), not on its own code -- rebuild narrowly: test fixtures `polyglot-zsh-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.zsh` and `polyglot-fish-*.fish` with line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG|LYR-..>-<data>` and each plausible descriptor form: zsh `typeset -r descriptor_<8hex>=\\\"..\\\"`, `readonly DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>='..'`, `local -r`, `build_plan_<8hex>() { print -r -- \\\"..\\\" }` (function-return like D26 Erlang), `${(j::)parts}` joins of an array literal `parts=(..)`; fish `set -g descriptor_<8hex> \\\"..\\\"` (no `=`), `set -l`, `function build_plan_<8hex>; echo \\\"..\\\"; end`, `string join '' ..`. Assert lib.codec.v3_plan and the carried marker-routed solver return plan-verbatim language=zsh/fish, campaign ZSH-/FISH-<8hex>, host zsh-/fish-<10hex>.example.invalid, /tmp/huntress-<lang>/. Families `polyglot-zsh`/`polyglot-fish`. Stdlib only; never run zsh/fish.\"},\n266\t  {\"id\": \"awk-sed-minimal-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"awk and sed v=3 polyglots in the plain D23-D26 shape (narrow re-queue of the given-up awk-sed-program-route)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"awk/sed are a sibling pair in the pool. awk-sed-program-route failed on a `__import__()` call (not allowed) and then on android xamarin_assembly_scan timing -- rebuild narrowly with plain imports. Fixtures: awk `#!/usr/bin/awk -f` + `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `BEGIN { descriptor_<8hex> = \\\"..\\\" }` or `function build_plan_<8hex>() { return \\\"..\\\" }`, juxtaposition concat `\\\"ab\\\" \\\"cd\\\"`; sed `#!/bin/sed -f` / `#n` first line + `# HUNTRESS..` + `s/^.*$/<data>/` or `1i\\\\` / `a\\\\` text commands carrying the data, `y/abc/xyz/` transliteration. Assert marker-first plan recovery (data may contain `/` escaped as `\\\\/` inside s///) and plan-verbatim answers (language=awk/sed, AWK-/SED-<8hex>). Never run awk/sed on fixtures.\"},\n267\t  {\"id\": \"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\", \"concept\": \"Nim, Swift and Tcl string-literal forms that can hide the descriptor\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 night re-try (1st attempt failed ONLY on another lane's fixture timing: android/xam_blob_v1.json xamarin_assembly_scan 6.1 s under load). 3 of the 14 pool languages left after D26. All in the pool. Nim: `# ` / `#[ ]#` comments, `const descriptorX = \\\"..\\\"`, `let`, raw `r\\\"..\\\"`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `&` concat, `\\\\x41` escapes, `import osproc` + `execProcess`/`startProcess`. Swift: `#!/usr/bin/swift`, `//` + `/* */`, `let descriptor_x: String = \\\"..\\\"`, raw `#\\\"..\\\"#`, multi-line `\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `\\\\u{41}`, `String(decoding: bytes, as: UTF8.self)`, `Process()`/`launchPath`. Tcl: `# ` comments (only at command start), `set descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` / `set descriptor_x {..}` (no `=`), `append`, `binary decode base64`/`hex`, `[join $l \\\"\\\"]`, `exec`. Fold, then V3 peel; fixtures in both grammars.\"},\n268\t  {\"id\": \"function-return-literal-battery\", \"concept\": \"nameless descriptor literals (function-return / command-argument) across the 14 remaining pool languages, plus a marker-damaged fallback\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 NSIS (`StrCpy $0 \\\"..\\\"`) and D26 Erlang (`build_plan() -> \\\"<data>\\\".`) carried the data with NO descriptor name -- only the marker regex found it. A timed/next-day twist could split or drop the marker line. Prebuild a lib.codec fallback that collects every string literal >= 40 chars in any quote syntax (\\\"..\\\", '..', Tcl `{..}`, Lua `[[..]]`, heredocs, `r#\\\"..\\\"#`, Swift `#\\\"..\\\"#`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`), joins adjacent pieces, shape-peels each (max 4 layers) and accepts only `v=`; plus fixtures for each pool language's function-return form: Rust `fn build_plan() -> &'static str { \\\"..\\\" }`, Swift `func buildPlan() -> String { return \\\"..\\\" }`, Kotlin `fun buildPlan() = \\\"..\\\"`, BeanShell `String buildPlan() { return \\\"..\\\"; }`, Nim `proc buildPlan(): string = \\\"..\\\"`, Tcl `proc build_plan {} { return {..} }`, Makefile `define DESCRIPTOR`..`endef`, Dockerfile `LABEL huntress.descriptor=\\\"..\\\"`, XSLT `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>`, HCL `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = \\\"..\\\" }`. Test: same plan with and without the marker line. Must stay inside the 2 s find_codecs fixture budget (gate on cheap substring/length tests).\"},\n269\t  {\"id\": \"cross-language-collision-decoys\", \"concept\": \"separate true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys (D26 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 prompt: 'some of its indicators look suspiciously familiar ... separate the true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys planted to look like old friends'. No decoy shipped, but a later question family could ask e.g. `<fam>-<stem>-true-indicator` / `-decoy-count` / `-handoff-target`. Prebuild lib.codec.indicator_collisions(plans_by_member) for ONE Mastery set: index every url/host/campaign/file_path/next_stage/handoff_id value; a TRUE cross-language link = value (or campaign token) that matches the consuming file's own plan AND the producer's `next_language`/next_stage member; a DECOY = same shape/prefix as an older language's indicator (e.g. `cdn-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `PSPY-<16HEX>`) whose token differs from the file's campaign token, or whose `<lang>-` host prefix disagrees with `language=`. Return both lists with reasons; resolve per set (D23 lesson). Fixtures: two plans sharing a url host, one decoy differing in one hex char.\"},\n270\t  {\"id\": \"erlang-beam-chunk-literals\", \"concept\": \"compiled BEAM (`.beam`) and escript-archive carriers: recover string/binary literals statically\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 shipped Erlang source only. A timed/host twist could ship the compiled module or an escript with an embedded archive (`#!/usr/bin/env escript` + `%%! -escript main x` + a zip/beam payload after the header lines). Parse `FOR1 <len> BEAM` IFF chunks with struct: `AtU8`/`Atom` atoms, `StrT` string table, `LitT` (4-byte uncompressed size + zlib) holding External Term Format literals (tags 107 STRING_EXT, 109 BINARY_EXT, 108 LIST_EXT, 97/98 ints, 104/105 tuples, 119/118 atoms) -- hand-roll an ETF reader, no erlang on box; for escript archives skip the first 3 text lines and open the rest with zipfile. Feed every recovered string to lib.codec.v3_plan. Stdlib only (struct, zlib, zipfile).\"},\n271\t  {\"id\": \"shell-rc-host-carriers\", \"concept\": \"shell startup/config files as v=3 HOST profiles for zsh/fish/bash (persistence-flavoured hosts)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Hosts have shipped on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix) and none on D23/D26. If zsh/fish ship, a host is likely a startup file: `.zshrc`/`.zshenv`/`.zprofile`, oh-my-zsh `*.plugin.zsh`, `~/.config/fish/config.fish`, `conf.d/*.fish`, autoload `functions/<name>.fish`, bash `.bashrc`/`.profile` (T1546.004 Unix shell configuration modification). Expected host_profile spellings follow `<platform>_<kind>` (guess list for fixtures only: `zsh_rc`, `oh_my_zsh_plugin`, `fish_config`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside a function/alias/`precmd` hook, plus `source`/`autoload -Uz` lines that must be ignored. Assert routing by marker, not by file name.\"},\n272\t  {\"id\": \"jvm-pair-host-profiles\", \"concept\": \"BeanShell/Kotlin host carriers: JMeter `.jmx` samplers, Gradle Kotlin DSL, `.main.kts`\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"beanshell and kotlin are the JVM pair still in the pool (kotlin-beanshell-literal-route built the plain literal forms). Likely hosts: JMeter test plan XML `<BeanShellSampler>`/`<JSR223Sampler>` with `<stringProp name=\\\"BeanShellSampler.query\\\">` or `name=\\\"script\\\"` holding the script XML-escaped (`&quot;`, `&#xa;`) -> unescape then rescan (like D19 ASPX nesting); BeanShell in Burp/Ghidra/`bsh.Interpreter.eval(\\\"..\\\")`; Kotlin `build.gradle.kts`/`settings.gradle.kts` (`tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { exec { commandLine(..) } } }`), `.main.kts` with `@file:DependsOn(..)`. Fixtures: marker in `<!-- -->` or `//`, descriptor escaped inside the XML property. Stdlib xml.etree only (never resolve entities from DTDs).\"},\n273\t  {\"id\": \"stage-config-survival-diff\", \"concept\": \"config that changes shape across a stage chain and the key that 'didn't survive' (D25 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"1st attempt rejected: `import tomllib` is not in hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS -- hand-roll the TOML/sys.config/.exs keyword readers. D25 prompt: 'Configuration starts out in Elixir source and has changed shape by the time an inert Phoenix-hosted stage picks it up. Follow every transformation, reconcile each one with earlier campaign artifacts, and find the setting that didn't survive.' Nothing shipped, but a host day could ship it. lib.codec.config_chain(members) -> ordered [(member, format, {key: value})] parsing Elixir `config :app, Key, k: v` keyword lists / `%{}` maps / `runtime.exs` `System.get_env(\\\"X\\\", \\\"default\\\")`, Erlang `sys.config` terms `[{app, [{k, v}]}].`, `vm.args` `-k v`, `.env` `K=V`, JSON/YAML/TOML, plus every v=3 plan (`k=v|..`); key normalisation (snake/camel/upper, `:atom`, `\\\"str\\\"`); config_diff(chain) -> keys dropped / renamed / value-changed between consecutive stages and vs the corpus plan of the same campaign_id. Answer shapes to expect: the dropped KEY name verbatim, its last value, or the member where it vanished. Stdlib only; hand-rolled term parser (no ast).\"},\n274\t  {\"id\": \"actor-message-flow-model\", \"concept\": \"actor/message-passing flow from source (Erlang/Elixir spawn-send-receive, workers, channels) -- D26 prompt\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 asked to 'trace the message flow' between processes; the fixture had no message code. If a later host ships it: static edge list from Erlang `Pid = spawn(fun ..)`/`spawn(M, F, A)`, `register(name, Pid)`, `Pid ! {Tag, Value}`, `receive {Tag, X} -> ..`, `gen_server:call/cast` + `handle_call/handle_cast`; Elixir `send(pid, msg)`, `GenServer.call`, `Task.async`; JS `postMessage`/`onmessage`; Go `ch <- v` / `<-ch`. Output ordered (sender, receiver, tag, payload) tuples and the final consumer of each indicator; answer-ids would likely be new suffixes -> lib.codec.plan_answer first. Regex-based, stdlib only; never run erl/elixir.\"},\n275\t  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"read the timed plans' next_language pool as the forecast of upcoming languages\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"3/3 hits: D23 pool had jsp -> D24 JSP; D24 pool had elixir -> D25 Elixir; D25 pool had erlang -> D26 Erlang; each day's pool lost exactly that language. 14 left for 5 days (D27-D31): awk, beanshell, dockerfile, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh. The last two drops were siblings (BEAM); remaining sibling pairs: zsh/fish, awk/sed, dockerfile/makefile, kotlin/beanshell. Recompute nightly from every auto-* expected.json `-next-language` value and set the matching route gap to priority 1.\"},\n276\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try). D25: 9 sets, stems again identical across sets (`a7470f.exs` set1..set9); first try.\"},\n277\t  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens). D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape. D25: unchanged a 3rd time (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65 elixir ids).\"},\n278\t  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D25: the D25 solve.py (byte-identical D23/D24 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n279\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n280\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n281\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n282\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp .exs (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n283\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n284\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file. D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members). D25: `polyglot-elixir` (campaign ELIXIR-, url host elixir-.., /tmp/huntress-elixir/) + host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (profile elixir_phoenix); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-elixir` (5 members).\"},\n285\t  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n286\t  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n287\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n288\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n289\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n290\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n291\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n292\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n293\t]\n294\t```\n295\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78a6e362-6162-44c7-b7e9-4a571227269a","uuid":"71059793-48fa-49ff-b66b-3711965a718e","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:07:07.811Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md","content":"| 101 | Actor/message-passing flow (Erlang `spawn`/`!`/`receive`, Elixir `send`/`GenServer.call/cast`, Akka `tell`, Go channels, JS `postMessage`/Worker) | gap (D26 prompt \"trace the message flow\"; no code shipped) | `spawn(fun ..)`, `Pid ! {tag, V}`, `receive {tag, X} ->`, `register(name, Pid)`, `gen_server:call`, `handle_cast`; `send(pid, msg)`; `new Worker(`/`onmessage` | gap actor-message-flow-model (static send/receive edge list -> ordered flow) | low |\n\nCounts: 101 rows; seen 37 (rows 1-18, 22, 30 (GHA only), 35, 48-52, 67, 70, 75, 77 (JSP D24; Java/Kotlin gap), 82 (NSIS D22), 89-91 + 94\n(D23), 95 (Elixir D25, Erlang D26)), gap 64 (rows 100-101 opened by D26; rows 96-99 by D24; rows 66, 68, 69, 71, 72, 78-81, 83-86, 88, 92-93, 98-99 have lib support built; 87 given up).\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nFINGERPRINT (first 512 bytes + `file`), never by extension:\n FF FE / FE FF / NUL every 2nd byte -> UTF-16: iconv -f UTF-16LE -t UTF-8 first (.reg, PS \"Unicode\" saves, .inf)\n 1F 8B gzip | PK\\x03\\x04 zip/ooxml(.docm .xlsm) | D0 CF 11 E0 OLE(.doc .xls .msi) | ITSF chm | 4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 lnk\n E4 52 5C 7B onenote | \\x1bLua luac | FasdUAS .scpt | MEI\\x0c/PYZ pyinstaller | 0d0d0a pyc | #@~^ Script-Encoder -> wshenc\nSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:\n #!..perl / use strict; / my $descriptor_ -> perl (D15)   DESCRIPTOR_<HEX> = / def build_plan_ / ->(_env) -> ruby (D16)\n #Requires AutoHotkey / x := \"..\" / Map( / ; comments -> autohotkey v2 (D17; family polyglot-auto_hotkey, underscore)\n onOpen_ / DocumentApp / HtmlService / showSidebar / UrlFetchApp -> Google Apps Script (D18; polyglot-google_apps_script)\n ExcelScript./Office.onReady -> Office add-in  \"manifest_version\" -> browser ext  set x \"v\"/proc -> tcl  x <- v -> R  := -> go\n fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   final String x= / def f = { -> / pipeline{ -> groovy (D20)\n BEGIN{ / getline -> awk              target:\\n\\tcmd / $(shell -> make     FROM / RUN -> Dockerfile\n on:/jobs:/runs-on: + `# HUNTRESS..` line 1 + env HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR (no id) -> GH Actions (D21; polyglot-github_actions)\n Name/OutFile/Section + StrCpy $0 \"..\" + `;` marker -> NSIS (D22)  [Setup]/[Code] -> Inno  <Wix>/CustomAction -> WiX/MSI\n stages: -> GitLab  pool: -> Azure  kind: -> k8s  - hosts: -> ansible  local-exec -> terraform  Editor 5.00 -> .reg  $CHICAGO$ -> .inf\n <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild   <%@ Page/runat=\"server\" -> ASPX (D19)   <%@ Language=VBScript %> -> classic ASP (D20)\n <%! String DESCRIPTOR_ -> JSP (D24)  `#`+descriptor_x = +%{..} -> elixir (D25)  `%`+-module(+build_plan() -> \"..\". (no name) -> erlang (D26)\n extends RefCounted / const X: String = / func f() -> Dictionary: / `#` marker -> GDScript (D23)  [gd_scene/[gd_resource -> Godot\n resource (script/source = \"escaped\")  GDPC -> .pck  label start:/init python: -> Ren'Py  game:GetService -> Luau  @\"..\" -> Squirrel\n host-<profile>-<lang> may wrap an OLD language (D20 classic_asp VBScript in a .vbs): marker first, plan says language=\n Sub AutoOpen/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA  =EXEC( -> XLM  __EventFilter -> MOF  #nullable/BuildPlan_ => -> csx (D19)  let/|> -> fsx\nPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n marker with NO data (D18 `:SPLIT`) -> plan = next multi-line literal ARRAY `[ \"FRAG-..\",\"..\",..].join(\"\")`: join, strip\n   `<TAG>-`, peel; other syntaxes: `\"\".join([..])` `-join @(..)` `table.concat({..})` `join('',..)` `Join(Array(..),\"\")`.\n marker data running into `\\n..` / descriptor `= \\\"..\\\"` (D19 ASPX: inner script is an ESCAPED string) -> unescape `\\n \\\" \\\\`\n   (`\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) first\n   (it read D18 + D19), then fix the read -- never walk role/attack enums or put a guessed value in a bulk POST.\n descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n D23 `LYR-<l1>_<l2>_<l3>-data` = ENCODE layers (b64 b32 hex rev frag): undo last-first; obfuscation answer = layer string\n copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code or a known list\nTIMED CONTRACT GRAMMAR (D23): ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` over `<6hex>.<ext>` members -> route by field; composite fields =\n labels joined by `|` in the question's order; indicator = first present in the question's order; campaign-token = after 1st\n `-`; url-host/path-leaf from plan url/file_path; cross-file ids (handoff-id) resolved PER MASTERY SET. Diff id grammar first.\n Still the grammar D26 (TT 1677, M 10 sets; new lang = +13 ids/member). NEXT LANGUAGE = the one leaving the timed pool (3/3).\nLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n XLM xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper | Python: exec->print under python3 -I, marshal->pycdc\n compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\nNEVER run the fixture's interpreter (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File), Deparse/`make -n` (they execute), XSLT, plan URLs.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS: read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`, `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch expansion =\n STATEMENT table (D15+), but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (D23). A carried label rejected on unchanged\n bytes = regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh AND the asking field.\nNETWORK/PROCESS/OUTLIER/WEBSHELL/CONFIG-DRIFT/MESSAGE-FLOW+COLLISION-DECOY prompts (D16-D26): flavour (13/13) unless a question ships;\n then lib.codec network_indicators+reconcile, download_graph; declared_spawns vs process_events -> reconcile_processes.\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..Erlang).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D24 nights (see git history) and D25 night\nfind-codecs-speed-gate, beam-erlang-elixir-route, rust-cargo-buildrs-route, terraform-hcl-function-fold, jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier,\nwebshell-request-primitive-model, eex-heex-template-carrier, game-archive-carriers. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static,\nevidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route, awk-sed-program-route,\ncomposite-label-field-regime -- the D25-night failures were mostly OTHER lanes' fixture timings under load (android\nlocal_store_scan 4.67 s, xamarin_assembly_scan 2.05-6.10 s > 2 s) plus `__import__()` and `import tomllib` (not in\nhctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS: use stdlib parsers already allowed, hand-roll TOML), so the pool-language pairs are\nre-queued under NEW narrow ids. Priority-1 order for D27: the pool sibling pairs (zsh/fish, awk/sed), the Nim/Swift/Tcl\nliteral forms, and the nameless-literal fallback (D22 NSIS + D26 Erlang had no descriptor name); then the D26 narrative\n(collision decoys), compiled BEAM, shell-rc and JVM host twists, the D25 config-survival model, message flow last.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"zsh-fish-minimal-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"zsh and fish v=3 polyglots in the plain D23-D26 shape (narrow re-queue of the given-up zsh-fish-shell-route)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"zsh/fish are a sibling pair still in the 14-language pool after D26 (the last two drops were the BEAM pair Elixir -> Erlang). zsh-fish-shell-route failed twice ONLY on android fixture timing (local_store_scan 4.67 s), not on its own code -- rebuild narrowly: test fixtures `polyglot-zsh-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.zsh` and `polyglot-fish-*.fish` with line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG|LYR-..>-<data>` and each plausible descriptor form: zsh `typeset -r descriptor_<8hex>=\\\"..\\\"`, `readonly DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>='..'`, `local -r`, `build_plan_<8hex>() { print -r -- \\\"..\\\" }` (function-return like D26 Erlang), `${(j::)parts}` joins of an array literal `parts=(..)`; fish `set -g descriptor_<8hex> \\\"..\\\"` (no `=`), `set -l`, `function build_plan_<8hex>; echo \\\"..\\\"; end`, `string join '' ..`. Assert lib.codec.v3_plan and the carried marker-routed solver return plan-verbatim language=zsh/fish, campaign ZSH-/FISH-<8hex>, host zsh-/fish-<10hex>.example.invalid, /tmp/huntress-<lang>/. Families `polyglot-zsh`/`polyglot-fish`. Stdlib only; never run zsh/fish.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"awk-sed-minimal-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"awk and sed v=3 polyglots in the plain D23-D26 shape (narrow re-queue of the given-up awk-sed-program-route)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"awk/sed are a sibling pair in the pool. awk-sed-program-route failed on a `__import__()` call (not allowed) and then on android xamarin_assembly_scan timing -- rebuild narrowly with plain imports. Fixtures: awk `#!/usr/bin/awk -f` + `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `BEGIN { descriptor_<8hex> = \\\"..\\\" }` or `function build_plan_<8hex>() { return \\\"..\\\" }`, juxtaposition concat `\\\"ab\\\" \\\"cd\\\"`; sed `#!/bin/sed -f` / `#n` first line + `# HUNTRESS..` + `s/^.*$/<data>/` or `1i\\\\` / `a\\\\` text commands carrying the data, `y/abc/xyz/` transliteration. Assert marker-first plan recovery (data may contain `/` escaped as `\\\\/` inside s///) and plan-verbatim answers (language=awk/sed, AWK-/SED-<8hex>). Never run awk/sed on fixtures.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\", \"concept\": \"Nim, Swift and Tcl string-literal forms that can hide the descriptor\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 night re-try (1st attempt failed ONLY on another lane's fixture timing: android/xam_blob_v1.json xamarin_assembly_scan 6.1 s under load). 3 of the 14 pool languages left after D26. All in the pool. Nim: `# ` / `#[ ]#` comments, `const descriptorX = \\\"..\\\"`, `let`, raw `r\\\"..\\\"`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `&` concat, `\\\\x41` escapes, `import osproc` + `execProcess`/`startProcess`. Swift: `#!/usr/bin/swift`, `//` + `/* */`, `let descriptor_x: String = \\\"..\\\"`, raw `#\\\"..\\\"#`, multi-line `\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `\\\\u{41}`, `String(decoding: bytes, as: UTF8.self)`, `Process()`/`launchPath`. Tcl: `# ` comments (only at command start), `set descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` / `set descriptor_x {..}` (no `=`), `append`, `binary decode base64`/`hex`, `[join $l \\\"\\\"]`, `exec`. Fold, then V3 peel; fixtures in both grammars.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"function-return-literal-battery\", \"concept\": \"nameless descriptor literals (function-return / command-argument) across the 14 remaining pool languages, plus a marker-damaged fallback\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 NSIS (`StrCpy $0 \\\"..\\\"`) and D26 Erlang (`build_plan() -> \\\"<data>\\\".`) carried the data with NO descriptor name -- only the marker regex found it. A timed/next-day twist could split or drop the marker line. Prebuild a lib.codec fallback that collects every string literal >= 40 chars in any quote syntax (\\\"..\\\", '..', Tcl `{..}`, Lua `[[..]]`, heredocs, `r#\\\"..\\\"#`, Swift `#\\\"..\\\"#`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`), joins adjacent pieces, shape-peels each (max 4 layers) and accepts only `v=`; plus fixtures for each pool language's function-return form: Rust `fn build_plan() -> &'static str { \\\"..\\\" }`, Swift `func buildPlan() -> String { return \\\"..\\\" }`, Kotlin `fun buildPlan() = \\\"..\\\"`, BeanShell `String buildPlan() { return \\\"..\\\"; }`, Nim `proc buildPlan(): string = \\\"..\\\"`, Tcl `proc build_plan {} { return {..} }`, Makefile `define DESCRIPTOR`..`endef`, Dockerfile `LABEL huntress.descriptor=\\\"..\\\"`, XSLT `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>`, HCL `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = \\\"..\\\" }`. Test: same plan with and without the marker line. Must stay inside the 2 s find_codecs fixture budget (gate on cheap substring/length tests).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cross-language-collision-decoys\", \"concept\": \"separate true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys (D26 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 prompt: 'some of its indicators look suspiciously familiar ... separate the true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys planted to look like old friends'. No decoy shipped, but a later question family could ask e.g. `<fam>-<stem>-true-indicator` / `-decoy-count` / `-handoff-target`. Prebuild lib.codec.indicator_collisions(plans_by_member) for ONE Mastery set: index every url/host/campaign/file_path/next_stage/handoff_id value; a TRUE cross-language link = value (or campaign token) that matches the consuming file's own plan AND the producer's `next_language`/next_stage member; a DECOY = same shape/prefix as an older language's indicator (e.g. `cdn-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `PSPY-<16HEX>`) whose token differs from the file's campaign token, or whose `<lang>-` host prefix disagrees with `language=`. Return both lists with reasons; resolve per set (D23 lesson). Fixtures: two plans sharing a url host, one decoy differing in one hex char.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"erlang-beam-chunk-literals\", \"concept\": \"compiled BEAM (`.beam`) and escript-archive carriers: recover string/binary literals statically\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 shipped Erlang source only. A timed/host twist could ship the compiled module or an escript with an embedded archive (`#!/usr/bin/env escript` + `%%! -escript main x` + a zip/beam payload after the header lines). Parse `FOR1 <len> BEAM` IFF chunks with struct: `AtU8`/`Atom` atoms, `StrT` string table, `LitT` (4-byte uncompressed size + zlib) holding External Term Format literals (tags 107 STRING_EXT, 109 BINARY_EXT, 108 LIST_EXT, 97/98 ints, 104/105 tuples, 119/118 atoms) -- hand-roll an ETF reader, no erlang on box; for escript archives skip the first 3 text lines and open the rest with zipfile. Feed every recovered string to lib.codec.v3_plan. Stdlib only (struct, zlib, zipfile).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"shell-rc-host-carriers\", \"concept\": \"shell startup/config files as v=3 HOST profiles for zsh/fish/bash (persistence-flavoured hosts)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Hosts have shipped on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix) and none on D23/D26. If zsh/fish ship, a host is likely a startup file: `.zshrc`/`.zshenv`/`.zprofile`, oh-my-zsh `*.plugin.zsh`, `~/.config/fish/config.fish`, `conf.d/*.fish`, autoload `functions/<name>.fish`, bash `.bashrc`/`.profile` (T1546.004 Unix shell configuration modification). Expected host_profile spellings follow `<platform>_<kind>` (guess list for fixtures only: `zsh_rc`, `oh_my_zsh_plugin`, `fish_config`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside a function/alias/`precmd` hook, plus `source`/`autoload -Uz` lines that must be ignored. Assert routing by marker, not by file name.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-pair-host-profiles\", \"concept\": \"BeanShell/Kotlin host carriers: JMeter `.jmx` samplers, Gradle Kotlin DSL, `.main.kts`\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"beanshell and kotlin are the JVM pair still in the pool (kotlin-beanshell-literal-route built the plain literal forms). Likely hosts: JMeter test plan XML `<BeanShellSampler>`/`<JSR223Sampler>` with `<stringProp name=\\\"BeanShellSampler.query\\\">` or `name=\\\"script\\\"` holding the script XML-escaped (`&quot;`, `&#xa;`) -> unescape then rescan (like D19 ASPX nesting); BeanShell in Burp/Ghidra/`bsh.Interpreter.eval(\\\"..\\\")`; Kotlin `build.gradle.kts`/`settings.gradle.kts` (`tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { exec { commandLine(..) } } }`), `.main.kts` with `@file:DependsOn(..)`. Fixtures: marker in `<!-- -->` or `//`, descriptor escaped inside the XML property. Stdlib xml.etree only (never resolve entities from DTDs).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stage-config-survival-diff\", \"concept\": \"config that changes shape across a stage chain and the key that 'didn't survive' (D25 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"1st attempt rejected: `import tomllib` is not in hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS -- hand-roll the TOML/sys.config/.exs keyword readers. D25 prompt: 'Configuration starts out in Elixir source and has changed shape by the time an inert Phoenix-hosted stage picks it up. Follow every transformation, reconcile each one with earlier campaign artifacts, and find the setting that didn't survive.' Nothing shipped, but a host day could ship it. lib.codec.config_chain(members) -> ordered [(member, format, {key: value})] parsing Elixir `config :app, Key, k: v` keyword lists / `%{}` maps / `runtime.exs` `System.get_env(\\\"X\\\", \\\"default\\\")`, Erlang `sys.config` terms `[{app, [{k, v}]}].`, `vm.args` `-k v`, `.env` `K=V`, JSON/YAML/TOML, plus every v=3 plan (`k=v|..`); key normalisation (snake/camel/upper, `:atom`, `\\\"str\\\"`); config_diff(chain) -> keys dropped / renamed / value-changed between consecutive stages and vs the corpus plan of the same campaign_id. Answer shapes to expect: the dropped KEY name verbatim, its last value, or the member where it vanished. Stdlib only; hand-rolled term parser (no ast).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"actor-message-flow-model\", \"concept\": \"actor/message-passing flow from source (Erlang/Elixir spawn-send-receive, workers, channels) -- D26 prompt\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 asked to 'trace the message flow' between processes; the fixture had no message code. If a later host ships it: static edge list from Erlang `Pid = spawn(fun ..)`/`spawn(M, F, A)`, `register(name, Pid)`, `Pid ! {Tag, Value}`, `receive {Tag, X} -> ..`, `gen_server:call/cast` + `handle_call/handle_cast`; Elixir `send(pid, msg)`, `GenServer.call`, `Task.async`; JS `postMessage`/`onmessage`; Go `ch <- v` / `<-ch`. Output ordered (sender, receiver, tag, payload) tuples and the final consumer of each indicator; answer-ids would likely be new suffixes -> lib.codec.plan_answer first. Regex-based, stdlib only; never run erl/elixir.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"read the timed plans' next_language pool as the forecast of upcoming languages\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"3/3 hits: D23 pool had jsp -> D24 JSP; D24 pool had elixir -> D25 Elixir; D25 pool had erlang -> D26 Erlang; each day's pool lost exactly that language. 14 left for 5 days (D27-D31): awk, beanshell, dockerfile, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh. The last two drops were siblings (BEAM); remaining sibling pairs: zsh/fish, awk/sed, dockerfile/makefile, kotlin/beanshell. Recompute nightly from every auto-* expected.json `-next-language` value and set the matching route gap to priority 1.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try). D25: 9 sets, stems again identical across sets (`a7470f.exs` set1..set9); first try.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens). D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape. D25: unchanged a 3rd time (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65 elixir ids).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D25: the D25 solve.py (byte-identical D23/D24 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp .exs (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file. D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members). D25: `polyglot-elixir` (campaign ELIXIR-, url host elixir-.., /tmp/huntress-elixir/) + host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (profile elixir_phoenix); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-elixir` (5 members).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":110,"startLine":186,"totalLines":295}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FWPPcPD6mekY6P1y1etLP8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
